    "response": "{\n  \"explanation\": \"The alert indicates a potential SQL Injection vulnerability in the JDBC prepareStatement call at line 97. The value of the SQL argument is constructed by concatenating user input from the query string with a static SQL statement. Specifically, the variable 'bar' which holds user input is directly concatenated into the SQL query string without being parameterized. This can lead to SQL Injection if an attacker manipulates the query string.\\n\\nThe verified_api indicates that the source of the data is from HttpServletRequest.getQueryString(). The Steps section shows how the query string is processed to extract a parameter value, which is then decoded and assigned to 'bar'. This 'bar' variable is directly included in the SQL query string at line 97. There are no indications of binding this user input to a placeholder in the prepareStatement call.\\n\\nThe Sink section shows the prepareStatement method being called with the constructed SQL string. The supporting excerpts confirm that the statement is executed without further processing of 'bar'.\\n\\nGiven these details, it appears that user input is directly included in the SQL query string, which could lead to SQL Injection.\",\n  \"citations\": [\n    {\n      \"file_id\": \"F0\",\n      \"line\": 97\n    },\n    {\n      \"file_id\": \"F0\",\n      \"line\": 43\n    }\n  ],\n  \"verdict\": \"LIKELY_TP\"\n}",
